    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d473">

                <pb facs="0431" n="424" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg424"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94111/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-16T14:00:00-04:00">August 16, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>152. Please telegraph me as soon as possible your estimate of the probable
                    reaction in China should the President decide to invoke the so-called Neutrality
                    Act of May 1, 1937.<anchor n="17" xml:id="d473-f1"/> Any further comments that
                    you may feel moved to offer on the question of the advisability of the President
                    taking such action would be welcomed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
